var documenterSearchIndex = {"docs":
[{"category":"section","location":"api/shaping/#Shaping","page":"Shaping","text":"Text shaping is the core operation: given a font and a string, HarfBuzz produces a sequence of glyph IDs, cluster mappings, and positions.","title":"Shaping"},{"category":"section","location":"api/shaping/#Features","page":"Shaping","text":"Three spellings are accepted, each with a distinct job. 0 disables a feature, 1 enables it, higher values select an alternate.\n\n# 1. HarfBuzz's own syntax -- the canonical form, and the only one that\n#    expresses everything. Same syntax as `hb-shape --features`.\nHB.shape(font, \"AVATAR\"; features = [\"kern=0\"])\nHB.shape(font, \"office\"; features = [\"-liga\"])\nHB.shape(font, \"hello\";  features = [\"aalt[3:5]=2\"])     # over a range\n\n# 2. Pairs, for the common global case.\nHB.shape(font, \"hello\";  features = [\"smcp\" => 1])\n\n# 3. `Feature` values, for features built programmatically.\nHB.shape(font, \"hello\";  features = [HB.Feature(\"aalt\", 2, 3, 5)])\n\nDict and NamedTuple are deliberately not accepted. Features apply in order — the last entry for a tag wins — and the same tag may appear more than once over different ranges:\n\nHB.shape(font, text; features = [\"kern[0:2]=0\", \"kern[2:6]=1\"])\n\nA Dict is unordered and neither it nor a NamedTuple can hold a repeated tag or a range, so both would silently drop capability.","title":"Features"},{"category":"section","location":"api/shaping/#Glyph-flags","page":"Shaping","text":"A shaped run cannot always be split at an arbitrary glyph: breaking inside a cluster the shaper joined would change the result. These predicates are what a line breaker consults.","title":"Glyph flags"},{"category":"section","location":"api/shaping/#Result-accessors","page":"Shaping","text":"","title":"Result accessors"},{"category":"section","location":"api/shaping/#Shapers","page":"Shaping","text":"","title":"Shapers"},{"category":"function","location":"api/shaping/#HarfBuzz.shape","page":"Shaping","text":"shape(font::Font, text::AbstractString;\n      features = nothing, shapers = nothing) -> ShapeResult\n\nOne-shot convenience: create a buffer, add text, guess segment properties, shape, and return the result.\n\nresult = shape(font, \"Hello\")\nresult = shape(font, \"AVATAR\"; features = [\"kern=0\"])\nresult = shape(font, \"AVATAR\"; features = [\"kern\" => 0])\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"HarfBuzz.shape"},{"category":"function","location":"api/shaping/#HarfBuzz.shape!","page":"Shaping","text":"shape!(font::Font, buf::Buffer; features = nothing, shapers = nothing)\n\nShape the text in buf using font. Returns a ShapeResult with glyph infos and positions.\n\nfeatures accepts HarfBuzz feature strings, \"tag\" => value pairs, or Feature values. shapers restricts which backends may be tried, in order; see shapers for the available names. Shaping raises an error when no listed shaper can handle the buffer.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"HarfBuzz.shape!"},{"category":"type","location":"api/shaping/#HarfBuzz.Feature","page":"Shaping","text":"Feature(tag, value, start, stop)\nFeature(spec::AbstractString)\n\nAn OpenType feature to apply while shaping: a 4-byte tag, a value (0 disables, 1 enables, higher values select an alternate), and the half-open buffer range [start, stop) it applies to.\n\nThe string form is HarfBuzz's own syntax, the same one hb-shape --features takes:\n\nFeature(\"kern\")         # kern=1, whole buffer\nFeature(\"-liga\")        # liga=0\nFeature(\"aalt[3:5]=2\")  # aalt=2, over items 3 to 5\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"HarfBuzz.Feature"},{"category":"function","location":"api/shaping/#HarfBuzz.unsafe_to_break","page":"Shaping","text":"unsafe_to_break(info::GlyphInfo) -> Bool\n\nTrue when breaking the text at the start of this glyph's cluster would change the shaping result, so both halves would need reshaping. This is what a line breaker must consult before splitting a shaped run.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"HarfBuzz.unsafe_to_break"},{"category":"function","location":"api/shaping/#HarfBuzz.unsafe_to_concat","page":"Shaping","text":"unsafe_to_concat(info::GlyphInfo) -> Bool\n\nTrue when this glyph's cluster cannot be concatenated with what precedes or follows without reshaping. Only reported when the buffer carries the :produce_unsafe_to_concat flag.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"HarfBuzz.unsafe_to_concat"},{"category":"function","location":"api/shaping/#HarfBuzz.safe_to_insert_tatweel","page":"Shaping","text":"safe_to_insert_tatweel(info::GlyphInfo) -> Bool\n\nTrue when an Arabic tatweel may be inserted at this position without changing the shaping. Only reported when the buffer carries the :produce_safe_to_insert_tatweel flag.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"HarfBuzz.safe_to_insert_tatweel"},{"category":"function","location":"api/shaping/#HarfBuzz.glyph_ids","page":"Shaping","text":"glyph_ids(result::ShapeResult) -> Vector{UInt32}\n\nReturn the glyph IDs from a ShapeResult.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"HarfBuzz.glyph_ids"},{"category":"function","location":"api/shaping/#HarfBuzz.clusters","page":"Shaping","text":"clusters(result::ShapeResult) -> Vector{UInt32}\n\nReturn the cluster indices from a ShapeResult. Each cluster index corresponds to the byte offset in the original UTF-8 input string of the glyph sequence it belongs to.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"HarfBuzz.clusters"},{"category":"function","location":"api/shaping/#HarfBuzz.px","page":"Shaping","text":"px(v) -> Float64\n\nConvert a 26.6 fixed-point value – the unit of every advance and offset in a ShapeResult – to pixels.\n\npx(694)   # 10.84375\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"HarfBuzz.px"},{"category":"function","location":"api/shaping/#HarfBuzz.shapers","page":"Shaping","text":"shapers() -> Vector{String}\n\nNames of the shaping backends this build supports, in the order HarfBuzz would try them. \"ot\" is the OpenType shaper and is always present.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"HarfBuzz.shapers"},{"category":"section","location":"api/types/#Types","page":"Types","text":"Nothing is exported: Font, Face, Buffer and Blob are far too generic to place in your namespace. Reach them through the module.\n\nimport HarfBuzz as HB\n\nface = HB.Face(\"/System/Library/Fonts/Menlo.ttc\")\nfont = HB.Font(face; size = 18)","title":"Types"},{"category":"section","location":"api/types/#Object-chain","page":"Types","text":"HarfBuzz stacks three objects: a Blob holds bytes, a Face interprets them as font tables, and a Font fixes a size. Each keeps the one below it alive, so a Font built straight from a path is self-sufficient.","title":"Object chain"},{"category":"section","location":"api/types/#Buffers","page":"Types","text":"","title":"Buffers"},{"category":"section","location":"api/types/#Result-types","page":"Types","text":"","title":"Result types"},{"category":"type","location":"api/types/#HarfBuzz.Blob","page":"Types","text":"Blob(path::AbstractString)\nBlob(data::AbstractVector{UInt8})\n\nA chunk of binary data, usually the contents of a font file. Blob is the bottom of HarfBuzz's object chain: a Face is created from a blob, and a Font from a face.\n\nCreating a blob from a Julia array does not copy it; the array is kept alive by the blob.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"HarfBuzz.Blob"},{"category":"type","location":"api/types/#HarfBuzz.Face","page":"Types","text":"Face(blob::Blob; index::Integer = 0)\nFace(path::AbstractString; index::Integer = 0)\n\nA font face: the tables of one font inside a Blob. index selects the face inside a TrueType Collection.\n\nA face carries no size; combine it with a size to get a Font.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"HarfBuzz.Face"},{"category":"type","location":"api/types/#HarfBuzz.Font","page":"Types","text":"Font(face::Face; size = nothing, scale = nothing, funcs = :ot)\nFont(path::AbstractString; size, index = 0, funcs = :ot)\nFont(family::AbstractString; size)\n\nA face at a given size, ready to shape.\n\nsize is in pixels and sets the scale to size * 64, so advances and offsets come back in 26.6 fixed point; use px to convert them. scale sets the scale directly, in font units, and takes precedence.\n\nfuncs selects where glyph metrics come from:\n\n:ot (default) – HarfBuzz reads the font tables itself. No FreeType.\n:freetype – metrics come from FreeType, matching its hinting and rounding. Requires using FreeType, which loads the extension.\n\npath must be a font file. HarfBuzz has no font database, and neither does this package: resolve family names with Fontconfig.jl, FreeTypeAbstraction.jl or a platform API, then pass the path.\n\nfont = Font(\"/System/Library/Fonts/Menlo.ttc\"; size = 18)\nfont = Font(face; scale = (2048, 2048))\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"HarfBuzz.Font"},{"category":"type","location":"api/types/#HarfBuzz.Buffer","page":"Types","text":"Buffer()\n\nCreate an empty buffer. Add text with add_text!, then call shape!.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"HarfBuzz.Buffer"},{"category":"type","location":"api/types/#HarfBuzz.GlyphInfo","page":"Types","text":"GlyphInfo\n\nPer-glyph output from shaping. Fields:\n\nglyph_id::UInt32 — glyph ID in the font. Before shaping this is the input codepoint instead.\ncluster::UInt32 — byte offset of the originating cluster in the input UTF-8 text.\nflags::UInt32 — see unsafe_to_break and unsafe_to_concat.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"HarfBuzz.GlyphInfo"},{"category":"type","location":"api/types/#HarfBuzz.GlyphPosition","page":"Types","text":"GlyphPosition\n\nPer-glyph position from shaping. All fields are in the font's scale units, which Font's size argument sets to 26.6 fixed point (1/64 px); convert with px. Fields:\n\nx_advance::Int32, y_advance::Int32 — advance to the next glyph.\nx_offset::Int32, y_offset::Int32 — offset from the pen position.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"HarfBuzz.GlyphPosition"},{"category":"type","location":"api/types/#HarfBuzz.ShapeResult","page":"Types","text":"ShapeResult\n\nResult of shape / shape!. Fields:\n\ninfos::Vector{GlyphInfo} — one entry per output glyph.\npositions::Vector{GlyphPosition} — parallel to infos.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"HarfBuzz.ShapeResult"},{"category":"section","location":"api/queries/#Font-queries","page":"Font queries","text":"","title":"Font queries"},{"category":"section","location":"api/queries/#Library","page":"Font queries","text":"","title":"Library"},{"category":"section","location":"api/queries/#Blob-contents","page":"Font queries","text":"","title":"Blob contents"},{"category":"section","location":"api/queries/#Face-metadata","page":"Font queries","text":"","title":"Face metadata"},{"category":"section","location":"api/queries/#Font-size-and-metrics-state","page":"Font queries","text":"scale, ppem and ptem each have a setter suffixed with ! (scale!, ppem!, ptem!).","title":"Font size and metrics state"},{"category":"section","location":"api/queries/#Glyph-availability","page":"Font queries","text":"","title":"Glyph availability"},{"category":"function","location":"api/queries/#HarfBuzz.version","page":"Font queries","text":"version() -> VersionNumber\n\nVersion of the HarfBuzz library being called.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"HarfBuzz.version"},{"category":"function","location":"api/queries/#HarfBuzz.version_string","page":"Font queries","text":"version_string() -> String\n\nVersion of the HarfBuzz library as it reports it.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"HarfBuzz.version_string"},{"category":"function","location":"api/queries/#HarfBuzz.tag","page":"Font queries","text":"tag(name::AbstractString) -> UInt32\n\nPack a four-character tag such as \"kern\" or \"GSUB\" into an hb_tag_t. Shorter names are padded with spaces, longer ones are truncated.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"HarfBuzz.tag"},{"category":"function","location":"api/queries/#HarfBuzz.tag_string","page":"Font queries","text":"tag_string(t::UInt32) -> String\n\nThe four characters of a tag.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"HarfBuzz.tag_string"},{"category":"function","location":"api/queries/#HarfBuzz.data","page":"Font queries","text":"data(blob::Blob) -> Vector{UInt8}\n\nCopy the blob's contents into a Julia array.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"HarfBuzz.data"},{"category":"function","location":"api/queries/#HarfBuzz.face_count","page":"Font queries","text":"face_count(blob::Blob) -> Int\n\nNumber of faces in the font file the blob holds. Greater than one for a TrueType Collection (.ttc).\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"HarfBuzz.face_count"},{"category":"function","location":"api/queries/#HarfBuzz.upem","page":"Font queries","text":"upem(face::Face) -> Int\n\nUnits per em: the design grid the face's outlines are expressed in, typically 1000 (CFF) or 2048 (TrueType).\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"HarfBuzz.upem"},{"category":"function","location":"api/queries/#HarfBuzz.glyph_count","page":"Font queries","text":"glyph_count(face::Face) -> Int\n\nNumber of glyphs in the face.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"HarfBuzz.glyph_count"},{"category":"function","location":"api/queries/#HarfBuzz.face_index","page":"Font queries","text":"face_index(face::Face) -> Int\n\nIndex of this face inside its collection.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"HarfBuzz.face_index"},{"category":"function","location":"api/queries/#HarfBuzz.table_tags","page":"Font queries","text":"table_tags(face::Face) -> Vector{String}\n\nThe four-character tags of every table in the face, e.g. \"cmap\", \"GSUB\", \"glyf\".\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"HarfBuzz.table_tags"},{"category":"function","location":"api/queries/#HarfBuzz.reference_table","page":"Font queries","text":"reference_table(face::Face, tag::AbstractString) -> Blob\n\nThe raw bytes of one table, as a blob. A table the face does not have yields an empty blob rather than an error.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"HarfBuzz.reference_table"},{"category":"function","location":"api/queries/#HarfBuzz.scale","page":"Font queries","text":"scale(font::Font) -> Tuple{Int,Int}\nscale!(font::Font, (x, y))\n\nGet or set the horizontal and vertical scale, in font units. Shaping output is expressed in these units.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"HarfBuzz.scale"},{"category":"function","location":"api/queries/#HarfBuzz.ppem","page":"Font queries","text":"ppem(font::Font) -> Tuple{Int,Int}\nppem!(font::Font, (x, y))\n\nGet or set the horizontal and vertical pixels-per-em, used by fonts that carry bitmap strikes or size-specific hinting.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"HarfBuzz.ppem"},{"category":"function","location":"api/queries/#HarfBuzz.ptem","page":"Font queries","text":"ptem(font::Font) -> Float64\nptem!(font::Font, points)\n\nGet or set the point size, which fonts with an optical size axis use to pick an optical variant. Zero means unset.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"HarfBuzz.ptem"},{"category":"function","location":"api/queries/#HarfBuzz.has_glyph","page":"Font queries","text":"has_glyph(font::Font, unicode::UInt32) -> Bool\n\nTrue if the font contains a glyph for unicode.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"HarfBuzz.has_glyph"},{"category":"function","location":"api/queries/#HarfBuzz.get_nominal_glyph","page":"Font queries","text":"get_nominal_glyph(font::Font, unicode::UInt32) -> UInt32\n\nReturn the glyph ID for a Unicode codepoint, or 0 if the font does not contain it.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"HarfBuzz.get_nominal_glyph"},{"category":"section","location":"#HarfBuzz.jl","page":"Home","text":"A Julia wrapper for the HarfBuzz text shaping library, built on HarfBuzz_jll.","title":"HarfBuzz.jl"},{"category":"section","location":"#Why","page":"Home","text":"ImGui (and its Julia binding CImGui.jl) draws each Unicode codepoint independently — there is no text shaping step. This means ligatures (such as the regional-indicator pair 🇫🇷 → French flag) and ZWJ sequences (👨‍👩‍👧‍👦) do not render correctly. HarfBuzz.jl provides the shaping step that fills this gap.","title":"Why"},{"category":"section","location":"#Quick-start","page":"Home","text":"Nothing is exported — Font, Face and Buffer are too generic to put in your namespace — so import the module under a short alias.\n\nimport HarfBuzz as HB\n\nfont = HB.Font(\"/System/Library/Fonts/Menlo.ttc\"; size = 18)\n\nresult = HB.shape(font, \"Hello 漢字 🇫🇷\")\nfor (info, pos) in zip(result.infos, result.positions)\n    println(\"glyph=$(info.glyph_id) cluster=$(info.cluster) \" *\n            \"advance=$(HB.px(pos.x_advance))px\")\nend\n\nHB.has_glyph(font, UInt32('A'))     # true\nHB.has_glyph(font, UInt32(0x6f22))  # false — Menlo lacks CJK","title":"Quick start"},{"category":"section","location":"#Object-chain","page":"Home","text":"Blob      raw bytes (a font file, or a Julia array)\n └─ Face  the font tables inside those bytes\n     └─ Font   a face at a given size, ready to shape\n\nEach object keeps the one below it alive, so the shorthands HB.Face(path) and HB.Font(path; size) are safe to use on their own.\n\nblob = HB.Blob(\"DejaVuSans.ttf\")\nface = HB.Face(blob)            # or HB.Face(path)\nfont = HB.Font(face; size = 18) # or HB.Font(path; size = 18)\n\nHB.upem(face)         # 2048\nHB.glyph_count(face)  # 6253\nHB.table_tags(face)   # [\"GDEF\", \"GPOS\", \"GSUB\", \"OS/2\", ...]","title":"Object chain"},{"category":"section","location":"#Sizes-and-units","page":"Home","text":"size is in pixels and sets the font scale to size * 64, so advances and offsets come back in 26.6 fixed point. HB.px converts them.\n\nfont = HB.Font(face; size = 18)\nHB.scale(font)                                       # (1152, 1152)\nHB.px(HB.shape(font, \"M\").positions[1].x_advance)    # 10.84375\n\nscale can also be set directly, in font units, which bypasses the pixel convenience entirely:\n\nfont = HB.Font(face; scale = (2048, 2048))","title":"Sizes and units"},{"category":"section","location":"#Metrics-backends","page":"Home","text":"By default HarfBuzz reads the font tables itself (hb_ot_font_set_funcs), so the package depends only on HarfBuzz_jll.\n\nFreeType is optional and lives behind a package extension:\n\nusing FreeType                  # loads the :freetype backend\nfont = HB.Font(face; size = 18, funcs = :freetype)\n\nWithout it, funcs = :freetype raises an ArgumentError naming the package to add.","title":"Metrics backends"},{"category":"section","location":"#Finding-a-font-file","page":"Home","text":"This package matches no font names. HarfBuzz has no font database, and neither do the other bindings — uharfbuzz, harfbuzz_rs and harfbuzzjs all take bytes or a path. Resolve the family name with a tool built for it, then pass the path:\n\nimport HarfBuzz as HB\n\nfont = HB.Font(\"/System/Library/Fonts/Menlo.ttc\"; size = 18)\n\nPassing anything that is not a file raises an ArgumentError saying so.\n\nKeeping matching out of the package also keeps it honest about cost: a family lookup means opening and scoring every font file on the machine unless the matcher caches, which is not something a shaping call should do behind your back.","title":"Finding a font file"},{"category":"section","location":"#API-overview","page":"Home","text":"Call Description\nHB.Blob(path) / HB.Blob(bytes) Wrap font bytes\nHB.Face(blob; index) A face inside those bytes\nHB.Font(face; size) A face at a size, ready to shape\nHB.shape(font, text) Shape text → ShapeResult\nHB.px(v) 26.6 fixed point → pixels\nHB.has_glyph(font, cp) Does the font cover this codepoint?\n\nSee the Types, Shaping, and Font queries pages for details.","title":"API overview"},{"category":"section","location":"api/buffers/#Buffers","page":"Buffers","text":"A buffer holds the text to shape, then the glyphs shaping produced. Its properties — direction, script, language — decide how the text is shaped, so set them (or let HarfBuzz guess) before calling shape!.\n\nimport HarfBuzz as HB\n\nbuf = HB.Buffer()\nHB.add_text!(buf, \"مرحبا\")\nHB.guess_segment_properties!(buf)\nHB.direction(buf)   # :rtl\nHB.script(buf)      # :Arab","title":"Buffers"},{"category":"section","location":"api/buffers/#Contents","page":"Buffers","text":"length(buf) gives the item count, isempty(buf) tests it, append!(dest, src) joins two buffers, and reverse!(buf) reverses the contents.","title":"Contents"},{"category":"section","location":"api/buffers/#Reading-a-buffer","page":"Buffers","text":"","title":"Reading a buffer"},{"category":"section","location":"api/buffers/#Properties","page":"Buffers","text":"","title":"Properties"},{"category":"section","location":"api/buffers/#Serialization","page":"Buffers","text":"Serializing is the practical way to write golden tests: shape, serialize, compare against a stored string — the same thing the hb-shape command-line tool prints.","title":"Serialization"},{"category":"section","location":"api/buffers/#Tracing","page":"Buffers","text":"","title":"Tracing"},{"category":"function","location":"api/buffers/#HarfBuzz.add_text!","page":"Buffers","text":"add_text!(buf::Buffer, text::AbstractString;\n          item_offset = 0, item_length = -1)\n\nAdd UTF-8 text to the buffer.\n\nThe whole string is always visible to the shaper as context, but only the bytes in [item_offset, item_offset + item_length) become items to shape. item_length = -1 means \"to the end\". Supplying context matters for scripts whose glyphs depend on their neighbours, such as Arabic: shaping a run without it produces the wrong contextual forms at the boundaries.\n\nOffsets are in bytes, matching the cluster values shaping returns.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"HarfBuzz.add_text!"},{"category":"function","location":"api/buffers/#HarfBuzz.add_codepoints!","page":"Buffers","text":"add_codepoints!(buf::Buffer, codepoints;\n                item_offset = 0, item_length = -1)\n\nAdd Unicode codepoints directly, bypassing UTF-8 decoding. Use this when the input is already decoded, or to feed HarfBuzz codepoints that are not valid on their own.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"HarfBuzz.add_codepoints!"},{"category":"function","location":"api/buffers/#HarfBuzz.clear!","page":"Buffers","text":"clear!(buf::Buffer)\n\nEmpty the buffer's contents, keeping direction, script, language and flags. Use reset! to drop those too.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"HarfBuzz.clear!"},{"category":"function","location":"api/buffers/#HarfBuzz.reset!","page":"Buffers","text":"reset!(buf::Buffer)\n\nReturn the buffer to its initial state: empty, with no direction, script, language or flags set.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"HarfBuzz.reset!"},{"category":"function","location":"api/buffers/#HarfBuzz.reverse_clusters!","page":"Buffers","text":"reverse_clusters!(buf::Buffer)\n\nReverse the buffer's contents, then reverse each cluster back, so cluster contents keep their order.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"HarfBuzz.reverse_clusters!"},{"category":"function","location":"api/buffers/#HarfBuzz.pre_allocate!","page":"Buffers","text":"pre_allocate!(buf::Buffer, size) -> Bool\n\nReserve room for size items up front. Returns false if the allocation failed.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"HarfBuzz.pre_allocate!"},{"category":"function","location":"api/buffers/#HarfBuzz.allocation_successful","page":"Buffers","text":"allocation_successful(buf::Buffer) -> Bool\n\nfalse once any allocation on this buffer has failed, which makes every later result unreliable.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"HarfBuzz.allocation_successful"},{"category":"function","location":"api/buffers/#HarfBuzz.glyph_infos","page":"Buffers","text":"glyph_infos(buf::Buffer) -> Vector{GlyphInfo}\n\nThe buffer's per-item information. Before shaping, glyph_id holds the input codepoint; after shaping, the glyph ID.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"HarfBuzz.glyph_infos"},{"category":"function","location":"api/buffers/#HarfBuzz.glyph_positions","page":"Buffers","text":"glyph_positions(buf::Buffer) -> Vector{GlyphPosition}\n\nThe buffer's per-glyph positions. Only meaningful after shaping.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"HarfBuzz.glyph_positions"},{"category":"function","location":"api/buffers/#HarfBuzz.codepoints","page":"Buffers","text":"codepoints(buf::Buffer) -> Vector{UInt32}\n\nThe buffer's input codepoints, before shaping replaces them with glyph IDs.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"HarfBuzz.codepoints"},{"category":"function","location":"api/buffers/#HarfBuzz.has_positions","page":"Buffers","text":"has_positions(buf::Buffer) -> Bool\n\nTrue once shaping has filled in position data.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"HarfBuzz.has_positions"},{"category":"function","location":"api/buffers/#HarfBuzz.direction","page":"Buffers","text":"direction(buf::Buffer) -> Symbol\ndirection!(buf::Buffer, dir::Symbol)\n\nText flow direction: :ltr, :rtl, :ttb, :btt, or :invalid when unset. guess_segment_properties! can infer it from the content.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"HarfBuzz.direction"},{"category":"function","location":"api/buffers/#HarfBuzz.script","page":"Buffers","text":"script(buf::Buffer) -> Symbol\nscript!(buf::Buffer, s::Symbol)\n\nWriting system, as an ISO 15924 tag such as :Latn, :Arab or :Hani.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"HarfBuzz.script"},{"category":"function","location":"api/buffers/#HarfBuzz.language","page":"Buffers","text":"language(buf::Buffer) -> String\nlanguage!(buf::Buffer, tag::AbstractString)\n\nBCP 47 language tag, e.g. \"en\", \"fr\", \"sr-latn\". Some features are language-specific.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"HarfBuzz.language"},{"category":"function","location":"api/buffers/#HarfBuzz.segment_properties","page":"Buffers","text":"segment_properties(buf::Buffer) -> NamedTuple\nsegment_properties!(buf::Buffer, props::NamedTuple)\n\nRead or set direction, script and language together. Any key left out of props is untouched.\n\nsegment_properties!(buf, (direction = :rtl, script = :Arab, language = \"ar\"))\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"HarfBuzz.segment_properties"},{"category":"function","location":"api/buffers/#HarfBuzz.guess_segment_properties!","page":"Buffers","text":"guess_segment_properties!(buf::Buffer)\n\nAsk HarfBuzz to guess script, language and direction from the buffer content.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"HarfBuzz.guess_segment_properties!"},{"category":"function","location":"api/buffers/#HarfBuzz.flags","page":"Buffers","text":"flags(buf::Buffer) -> Vector{Symbol}\nflags!(buf::Buffer, names)\n\nBuffer flags, as symbols. :bot and :eot tell the shaper the run is at the beginning or end of a paragraph, which affects contextual forms. :produce_unsafe_to_concat makes shaping report the extra glyph flag of the same name.\n\nAvailable: :bot, :eot, :preservedefaultignorables, :removedefaultignorables, :donotinsertdottedcircle, :verify, :produceunsafetoconcat, :producesafetoinsert_tatweel.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"HarfBuzz.flags"},{"category":"function","location":"api/buffers/#HarfBuzz.cluster_level","page":"Buffers","text":"cluster_level(buf::Buffer) -> Symbol\ncluster_level!(buf::Buffer, level::Symbol)\n\nHow finely shaping reports clusters: :monotone_graphemes (the default, clusters never decrease and whole graphemes stay together), :monotone_characters, or :characters (the finest, clusters may be in any order).\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"HarfBuzz.cluster_level"},{"category":"function","location":"api/buffers/#HarfBuzz.content_type","page":"Buffers","text":"content_type(buf::Buffer) -> Symbol\n\nWhat the buffer holds: :invalid when empty, :unicode after adding text, :glyphs after shaping.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"HarfBuzz.content_type"},{"category":"function","location":"api/buffers/#HarfBuzz.replacement_codepoint","page":"Buffers","text":"replacement_codepoint(buf::Buffer) -> UInt32\nreplacement_codepoint!(buf::Buffer, cp)\n\nCodepoint substituted for input bytes that are not valid UTF-8.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"HarfBuzz.replacement_codepoint"},{"category":"function","location":"api/buffers/#HarfBuzz.invisible_glyph","page":"Buffers","text":"invisible_glyph(buf::Buffer) -> UInt32\ninvisible_glyph!(buf::Buffer, gid)\n\nGlyph used for characters that should take space but draw nothing. Zero means the font's own space glyph.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"HarfBuzz.invisible_glyph"},{"category":"function","location":"api/buffers/#HarfBuzz.not_found_glyph","page":"Buffers","text":"not_found_glyph(buf::Buffer) -> UInt32\nnot_found_glyph!(buf::Buffer, gid)\n\nGlyph used for characters the font has no glyph for. Zero is .notdef.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"HarfBuzz.not_found_glyph"},{"category":"function","location":"api/buffers/#HarfBuzz.serialize","page":"Buffers","text":"serialize(buf::Buffer; font = nothing, format = :text, flags = Symbol[]) -> String\n\nRender the buffer's glyphs as text, in the same formats the hb-shape command-line tool produces. :text is the compact form (glyph=cluster+advance), :json an array of objects.\n\nfont is what turns glyph IDs into names; without it, glyphs are serialized by number. Flags: :noclusters, :nopositions, :noglyphnames, :glyphextents, :glyphflags, :no_advances.\n\nThis is the basis for golden tests: shape, serialize, compare to a stored string.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"HarfBuzz.serialize"},{"category":"function","location":"api/buffers/#HarfBuzz.deserialize!","page":"Buffers","text":"deserialize!(buf::Buffer, text::AbstractString;\n             font = nothing, format = :text) -> Buffer\n\nParse a serialized glyph list back into buf, the inverse of serialize.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"HarfBuzz.deserialize!"},{"category":"function","location":"api/buffers/#HarfBuzz.diff","page":"Buffers","text":"diff(reference::Buffer, other::Buffer;\n     dotted_circle_glyph = -1, position_fuzz = 0) -> Vector{Symbol}\n\nCompare two buffers. An empty result means they are equal; otherwise the symbols say how they differ, e.g. :length_mismatch, :codepoint_mismatch, :position_mismatch.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"HarfBuzz.diff"},{"category":"function","location":"api/buffers/#HarfBuzz.message_func!","page":"Buffers","text":"message_func!(buf::Buffer, f)\n\nCall f(message::String) at each stage of shaping this buffer – the same trace hb-shape --trace prints. Return false from f to skip the stage being announced. Pass nothing to remove the callback.\n\nThe buffer must stay alive for as long as the callback is installed.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"HarfBuzz.message_func!"}]
}
